<title>UK: UK's Clarke says to get inflation down to 2.5%.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke says to get inflation down to 2.5%.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said his annual budget was aimed at getting underlying inflation down to2.5 percent or less for the foreseeable future.</p>
<p>&quot;I expect underlying inflation to meet our target of 2-1/2 percent or less. I will ensure that it goes on meeting that target for the foreseeable future,&quot; he said in a speech to parliament on the 1997/98 budget.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7707</p>
